    "summary": "Your first journey through the southern states should introduce you to the region without trying to explain all of it in one holiday.",
    "relatedServiceSlug": "south-india-road-journeys",
    "content": "<p>Your first journey through the southern states should introduce you to the region without trying to explain all of it in one holiday.</p><p>If you are planning your first trip to South India, start with your interests.</p><p>Architecture enthusiasts might choose Hampi, Badami, Pattadakal or the temple cities of Tamil Nadu. Beach lovers could look towards Goa, Gokarna, coastal Karnataka or Kerala. Nature seekers have the Western Ghats, backwaters and wildlife destinations to consider.</p><p>Food can be a reason to travel too, particularly if you enjoy discovering regional cuisines.</p><p>Where should first-time visitors go in South India?</p><p>There is no single answer. Karnataka can offer a strong combination of heritage and landscapes. Tamil Nadu is ideal for travellers interested in temples and classical architecture. Kerala brings together backwaters, hills and coastal experiences, while Goa works well for travellers seeking beaches and leisure.</p><p>What is the biggest mistake first-time travellers make?</p><p>Trying to do everything.</p><p>A route that includes too many cities can leave you spending more time checking into hotels and sitting in traffic than actually experiencing the places.</p><p>Instead, choose a coherent circuit with a manageable number of stops.</p><p>A chauffeur-driven trip can make the first journey easier, especially when you are unfamiliar with the roads and distances.</p><p>Think of the holiday as an introduction.</p><p>You don't need to finish the entire map.</p><p>Leave with a few strong memories, a better understanding of the region and, ideally, a list of places you want to return to.</p><p>Your first trip doesn't need to be complete. It needs to make you curious.</p>"
